When you buy a car from a well-known brand like Ford, you expect complete reliability and minimal problems. Established in 1903, The Ford Motor Company has a long-standing reputation for quality in the auto industry, and has made some of the best cars on the market.

However, even reputable manufacturers can have a few issues slip through the cracks. Some Ford car defects are relatively minor, while others can be more serious and require immediate attention.

In this post, we’re going to explore the top ten most common defects found in Ford cars from different models. Whether you’re a Ford vehicle owner or considering becoming one, this list will give you a heads-up on what to watch out for.

## 1. Transmission Trouble

One of the most common defects in Ford cars is transmission problems. Models like the Ford Focus, Fiesta, and some Escape variants are known to experience jerky shifts, sudden acceleration, or even total transmission failure.

Apart from disrupting your driving experience, a malfunctioning transmission system can pose serious safety issues and lead to costly repairs. Worse still, if you’re constantly running back to the manufacturer with the same unresolved issue, you might have a lemon on your hands.

